        <li>show how the removal of an amino (or nitro) group from an aromatic ring through the reaction of an arenediazonium salt with hypophosphorous acid (H<sub>3</sub>PO<sub>2</sub>) can sometimes be of use in organic synthesis.</li>
    </ol>
    </li>
    <li>
